disabled the old remapped keys on each endpoint. Before/after captures
changed only for admitted controls, and release captures stabilized.
Private key files were removed. This establishes native keyboard
routing and persistence, not physical controllers or multi-device LAN.

Native TCP address-policy tests now cover private-range boundaries,
IPv6 unique-local and link-local addresses, public and multicast
addresses, and canonical IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses. Public and wildcard
binds and connects remain rejected. The same real mutual-TLS host
round-trip regression passes over IPv4, IPv6 and IPv4-mapped IPv6
loopback: schema rejection, valid frames and replies, reserved slots,
and same-identity rejoin. The Linux host has IPv6 loopback enabled;
these tests do not establish scoped link-local or multi-device routing.
Fresh validation passed in run 1795611541668604334-1069821.

The native controller now checks its acknowledgement lease before each
queued transport-send poll as well as before and after the bounded send
batch. A deterministic exact-boundary test queues a control on a real
mutual-TLS connection, rejects dispatch at lease expiry, and confirms
that only the disconnect reaches the host simulation. This cannot retract
bytes already submitted before expiry. Fresh validation passed in run
1795611697974351999-1098018.

Native SDL device-added notifications now schedule the same bounded
post-drain discovery used after removal, rather than opening a transient
joystick index from a queued notification. Only current enumerated
controllers receive stable attachment identities; pre-admission events
cannot act on a seat. Existing admitted button, axis and removal events
still use stable instance identifiers. The opt-in native render smoke
